📅 Day 48 – Introduction to Java Servlets

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on Java Servlets and their role in web application development. The mentor explained how servlets run on the server and handle client requests through a web container.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Introduction to Servlets
Servlets are Java programs that run on the server
Used to handle client requests and generate responses
Work within a web container (e.g., Apache Tomcat)
2️⃣ Servlet Lifecycle

The lifecycle of a servlet includes the following stages:

✅ init()
Called once when the servlet is initialized
Used for setup tasks
✅ service()
Handles client requests
Calls doGet() or doPost() methods
✅ destroy()
Called before the servlet is removed
Used for cleanup tasks
3️⃣ Request & Response Handling
HttpServletRequest → Receives client request
HttpServletResponse → Sends response to client
Used to generate dynamic web content
